00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.620
In Sim, chat is the fastest way to work
with your workspace when you know what you

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.780
want, but not necessarily what clicks it
will take to get there. Instead of jumping

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.960
between workflows, tables, files, and
knowledge bases yourself, you can ask from

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.780
one place and let chat reach across the
workspace for you. It can answer, operate,

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:26.340
and help shape the system around the task.
Let me show you what that feels like. This

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.900
is the chat in Sim. Everything in your
workspace is within its reach.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.220
Ask a question, and Sim queries your
tables and searches your documents at the

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.740
same time, then answers from both in one
reply.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.340
Tell it to act, and it runs your
workflows. Here, the whole backlog streams

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:51.260
through the support desk, while the weekly
digest goes out and lands on a schedule.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:59.400
It can reach outside the workspace, too,
searching this week's conversations on X

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.500
and Reddit. And filing what it learns back
in as a document.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.940
And the pieces compose, one sentence
builds a new workflow that reads those

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.420
trends on a schedule, and calls your
support desk when something matches.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.920
That's the chat in Sim. Open it. Ask for
what you need, and the workspace you've

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:22.460
already built does the work.
